{"text": "Dorothy L, Cheney, a renowned American biologist, is famous for her research on social relationships of non human primates like vervet monkeys and baboons. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Born in Boston in 1950, she graduated from Wellesley College in 1972. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although she originally planned to go to law school, her career plan changed after she joined her husband, Robert Seyfarth, for fieldwork on animal behavior. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Subsequently, she earned a doctoral degree in zoology from Cambridge University. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Between 1977 and 1988, she conducted field research in Kenya, discovering that vervet monkeys used different alarm calls for different predators such as leopards and snakes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Afterward, she carried out a project on baboons in Botswana. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cheney and her husband wrote Baboon Metaphysics, describing results from their fieldwork. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cheney had a strong influence on researchers of animal behavior, and many graduate students she mentored went on to distinguished careers in animal behavior.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "o", "r", "o", "t", "h", "y", " ", "L", ",", " ", "C", "h", "e", "n", "e", "y", ",", " ", "a", " ", "r", "e", "n", "o", "w", "n", "e", "d", " ", "A", "m", "e", "r", "i", "c", "a", "n", " ", "b", "i", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "s", "t", ",", " ", "i", "s", " ", "f", "a", "m", "o", "u", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "r", "e", "s", "e", "a", "r", "c", "h", " ", "o", "n", " ", "s", "o", "c", "i", "a", "l", " ", "r", "e", "l", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", "h", "i", "p", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "n", "o", "n", " ", "h", "u", "m", "a", "n", " ", "p", "r", "i", "m", "a", "t", "e", "s", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "v", "e", "r", "v", "e", "t", " ", "m", "o", "n", "k", "e", "y", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "b", "a", "b", "o", "o", "n", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"